      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Recommender Systems: Two-Tower, TFRS & Faiss ANN — Module 4 Specialization\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning Objectives\n",
        "- **Two-Tower Architecture**: Separate user/item encoders with dot-product similarity\n",
        "- **TensorFlow Recommenders (TFRS)**: End-to-end retrieval + ranking pipeline\n",
        "- **Faiss ANN**: Approximate Nearest Neighbor search for scalable retrieval\n",
        "- **Implicit Feedback**: Matrix factorization, BPR loss, weighted ALS\n",
        "- **Cold Start**: Content-based features, meta-learning, popularity fallback\n",
        "- **Evaluation**: Recall@K, NDCG@K, MAP, coverage, diversity\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters\n",
        "Recommender systems power discovery at Netflix, YouTube, Amazon, Spotify, TikTok. ML Architects must design two-stage systems: **retrieval** (candidate generation from millions) → **ranking** (precise scoring of hundreds). This notebook implements the full pipeline with real training and Faiss-based serving."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install required packages\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "!{sys.executable} -m pip install tensorflow-recommenders faiss-cpu pandas numpy matplotlib scikit-learn -q 2>/dev/null || true"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "import tensorflow_recommenders as tfrs\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import ndcg_score\n",
        "import faiss\n",
        "\n",
        "tf.random.set_seed(42)\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"TensorFlow: {tf.__version__}\")\n",
        "print(f\"TFRS: {tfrs.__version__}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Faiss: {faiss.__version__}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Synthetic Dataset: MovieLens-Style Interactions\n",
        "\n",
        "Generate realistic implicit feedback data with user/item features for content-based cold start."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Generate synthetic data\n",
        "n_users = 5000\n",
        "n_items = 2000\n",
        "n_interactions = 100000\n",
        "\n",
        "# User features\n",
        "user_ids = np.arange(n_users)\n",
        "user_age = np.random.randint(18, 70, n_users)\n",
        "user_gender = np.random.randint(0, 2, n_users)  # 0=F, 1=M\n",
        "user_genre_prefs = np.random.dirichlet(np.ones(10), n_users)  # 10 genres\n",
        "\n",
        "# Item features\n",
        "item_ids = np.arange(n_items)\n",
        "item_year = np.random.randint(1990, 2024, n_items)\n",
        "item_genres = np.random.dirichlet(np.ones(10), n_items)  # genre distribution\n",
        "item_popularity = np.random.zipf(2, n_items)  # long-tail popularity\n",
        "item_popularity = item_popularity / item_popularity.max() * 100\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate interactions (implicit feedback: watch, click, purchase)\n",
        "# Higher probability for items matching user genre preferences\n",
        "interactions = []\n",
        "for _ in range(n_interactions):\n",
        "    u = np.random.randint(0, n_users)\n",
        "    # Sample item weighted by popularity + preference match\n",
        "    prefs = user_genre_prefs[u]\n",
        "    match_scores = item_genres @ prefs\n",
        "    probs = (item_popularity + 1) * (match_scores + 0.1)\n",
        "    probs = probs / probs.sum()\n",
        "    i = np.random.choice(n_items, p=probs)\n",
        "    interactions.append((u, i))\n",
        "\n",
        "interactions = np.array(interactions)\n",
        "interactions_df = pd.DataFrame(interactions, columns=['user_id', 'item_id'])\n",
        "interactions_df['timestamp'] = np.random.randint(1609459200, 1704067200, n_interactions)\n",
        "interactions_df = interactions_df.drop_duplicates(subset=['user_id', 'item_id'])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Unique users: {interactions_df['user_id'].nunique()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Unique items: {interactions_df['item_id'].nunique()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Interactions: {len(interactions_df)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Sparsity: {1 - len(interactions_df) / (n_users * n_items):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Two-Tower Model Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "User Tower                    Item Tower\n",
        "┌─────────┐                   ┌─────────┐\n",
        "│ User ID │                   │ Item ID │\n",
        "└────┬────┘                   └────┬────┘\n",
        "     │                             │\n",
        "┌────▼────┐                   ┌────▼────┐\n",
        "│Embedding│                   │Embedding│\n",
        "└────┬────┘                   └────┬────┘\n",
        "     │                             │\n",
        "┌────▼────┐                   ┌────▼────┐\n",
        "│  Dense  │                   │  Dense  │\n",
        "│ Layers  │                   │ Layers  │\n",
        "└────┬────┘                   └────┬────┘\n",
        "     │                             │\n",
        "┌────▼────┐                   ┌────▼────┐\n",
        "│ User    │                   │ Item    │\n",
        "│ Vector  │                   │ Vector  │\n",
        "│  (64)   │                   │  (64)   │\n",
        "└────┬────┘                   └────┬────┘\n",
        "      \\                           /\n",
        "       \\                         /\n",
        "        \\                       /\n",
        "         ┌───────────────────┐\n",
        "         │   Dot Product     │\n",
        "         │   (Similarity)    │\n",
        "         └───────────────────┘\n",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Prepare TFRS dataset\n",
        "ratings = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices({\n",
        "    'user_id': interactions_df['user_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'item_id': interactions_df['item_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'timestamp': interactions_df['timestamp'].values.astype(np.int64)\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add user/item features\n",
        "users = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices({\n",
        "    'user_id': user_ids.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'age': user_age.astype(np.float32),\n",
        "    'gender': user_gender.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'genre_prefs': user_genre_prefs.astype(np.float32)\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "items = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices({\n",
        "    'item_id': item_ids.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'year': item_year.astype(np.float32),\n",
        "    'genres': item_genres.astype(np.float32),\n",
        "    'popularity': item_popularity.astype(np.float32)\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "# Vocabulary for StringLookup\n",
        "user_ids_vocab = user_ids.astype(str)\n",
        "item_ids_vocab = item_ids.astype(str)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Shuffle and split\n",
        "shuffled = ratings.shuffle(100000, seed=42, reshuffle_each_iteration=False)\n",
        "train = shuffled.take(80000)\n",
        "test = shuffled.skip(80000).take(20000)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Candidate set for retrieval (all items)\n",
        "candidates = items.batch(128)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Datasets prepared.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Retrieval Model (Two-Tower) with TFRS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# User model\n",
        "class UserModel(tf.keras.Model):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, embedding_dim=64):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.user_embedding = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.StringLookup(vocabulary=user_ids_vocab, mask_token=None),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Embedding(len(user_ids_vocab) + 1, embedding_dim)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        self.age_norm = tf.keras.layers.Normalization()\n",
        "        self.age_norm.adapt(users.map(lambda x: x['age']))\n",
        "        self.gender_embedding = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Embedding(2, 8)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        self.genre_dense = tf.keras.layers.Dense(32, activation='relu')\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.dense_layers = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(128, activation='relu'),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(embedding_dim)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def call(self, inputs):\n",
        "        user_id_emb = self.user_embedding(inputs['user_id'])\n",
        "        age_norm = tf.expand_dims(self.age_norm(inputs['age']), axis=1)\n",
        "        gender_emb = self.gender_embedding(inputs['gender'])\n",
        "        genre_emb = self.genre_dense(inputs['genre_prefs'])\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Concatenate all features\n",
        "        x = tf.concat([user_id_emb, age_norm, gender_emb, genre_emb], axis=1)\n",
        "        return self.dense_layers(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Item model\n",
        "class ItemModel(tf.keras.Model):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, embedding_dim=64):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.item_embedding = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.StringLookup(vocabulary=item_ids_vocab, mask_token=None),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Embedding(len(item_ids_vocab) + 1, embedding_dim)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        self.year_norm = tf.keras.layers.Normalization()\n",
        "        self.year_norm.adapt(items.map(lambda x: x['year']))\n",
        "        self.genre_dense = tf.keras.layers.Dense(32, activation='relu')\n",
        "        self.pop_norm = tf.keras.layers.Normalization()\n",
        "        self.pop_norm.adapt(items.map(lambda x: x['popularity']))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        self.dense_layers = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(128, activation='relu'),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(embedding_dim)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def call(self, inputs):\n",
        "        item_id_emb = self.item_embedding(inputs['item_id'])\n",
        "        year_norm = tf.expand_dims(self.year_norm(inputs['year']), axis=1)\n",
        "        genre_emb = self.genre_dense(inputs['genres'])\n",
        "        pop_norm = tf.expand_dims(self.pop_norm(inputs['popularity']), axis=1)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        x = tf.concat([item_id_emb, year_norm, genre_emb, pop_norm], axis=1)\n",
        "        return self.dense_layers(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "user_model = UserModel(64)\n",
        "item_model = ItemModel(64)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Test forward pass\n",
        "sample_user = next(iter(users.batch(2)))\n",
        "sample_item = next(iter(items.batch(2)))\n",
        "print(f\"User embedding shape: {user_model(sample_user).shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Item embedding shape: {item_model(sample_item).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# TFRS Retrieval Task\n",
        "class RetrievalModel(tfrs.Model):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, user_model, item_model):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.user_model = user_model\n",
        "        self.item_model = item_model\n",
        "        self.task = tfrs.tasks.Retrieval(\n",
        "            metrics=tfrs.metrics.FactorizedTopK(\n",
        "                candidates=candidates.map(item_model)\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def compute_loss(self, features, training=False):\n",
        "        user_emb = self.user_model({\n",
        "            'user_id': features['user_id'],\n",
        "            'age': features['age'] if 'age' in features else tf.zeros_like(features['user_id'], dtype=tf.float32),\n",
        "            'gender': features['gender'] if 'gender' in features else tf.zeros_like(features['user_id'], dtype=tf.int64),\n",
        "            'genre_prefs': features['genre_prefs'] if 'genre_prefs' in features else tf.zeros((tf.shape(features['user_id'])[0], 10))\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        \n",
        "        item_emb = self.item_model({\n",
        "            'item_id': features['item_id'],\n",
        "            'year': features['year'] if 'year' in features else tf.zeros_like(features['item_id'], dtype=tf.float32),\n",
        "            'genres': features['genres'] if 'genres' in features else tf.zeros((tf.shape(features['item_id'])[0], 10)),\n",
        "            'popularity': features['popularity'] if 'popularity' in features else tf.zeros_like(features['item_id'], dtype=tf.float32),\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        \n",
        "        return self.task(user_emb, item_emb, compute_metrics=not training)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Prepare training data with features\n",
        "def add_features(example):\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'user_id': example['user_id'],\n",
        "        'item_id': example['item_id'],\n",
        "        'age': tf.gather(user_age, example['user_id']),\n",
        "        'gender': tf.gather(user_gender, example['user_id']),\n",
        "        'genre_prefs': tf.gather(user_genre_prefs, example['user_id']),\n",
        "        'year': tf.gather(item_year, example['item_id']),\n",
        "        'genres': tf.gather(item_genres, example['item_id']),\n",
        "        'popularity': tf.gather(item_popularity, example['item_id']),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "train_with_features = train.map(add_features).batch(512).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
        "test_with_features = test.map(add_features).batch(512).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize model\n",
        "model = RetrievalModel(user_model, item_model)\n",
        "model.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adagrad(0.1))\n",
        "\n",
        "# Train retrieval model\n",
        "print(\"Training retrieval model...\")\n",
        "history = model.fit(train_with_features, epochs=3, verbose=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Evaluate\n",
        "print(\"\\nEvaluating retrieval...\")\n",
        "results = model.evaluate(test_with_features, return_dict=True, verbose=1)\n",
        "print(f\"Test metrics: {results}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Faiss Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN) Index\n",
        "\n",
        "For production serving, we need sub-millisecond retrieval from millions of items. Faiss provides GPU-accelerated ANN search."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Generate all item embeddings\n",
        "print(\"Generating item embeddings for Faiss index...\")\n",
        "all_item_embs = []\n",
        "for batch in items.batch(512):\n",
        "    emb = item_model(batch).numpy()\n",
        "    all_item_embs.append(emb)\n",
        "\n",
        "all_item_embs = np.vstack(all_item_embs).astype(np.float32)\n",
        "print(f\"Item embeddings shape: {all_item_embs.shape}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Normalize for cosine similarity (dot product on normalized = cosine)\n",
        "faiss.normalize_L2(all_item_embs)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Build Faiss index\n",
        "# IndexFlatIP: exact inner product (brute force)\n",
        "# IndexIVFFlat: inverted file with flat codes (approximate)\n",
        "# IndexHNSW: hierarchical navigable small world (best recall/speed)\n",
        "\n",
        "dim = all_item_embs.shape[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Exact index (for comparison)\n",
        "index_exact = faiss.IndexFlatIP(dim)\n",
        "index_exact.add(all_item_embs)\n",
        "\n",
        "# HNSW index (production choice)\n",
        "index_hnsw = faiss.IndexHNSWFlat(dim, 32)  # M=32 connections\n",
        "index_hnsw.hnsw.efConstruction = 80\n",
        "index_hnsw.hnsw.efSearch = 64\n",
        "index_hnsw.add(all_item_embs)\n",
        "\n",
        "# IVF index (for very large scale)\n",
        "nlist = 100\n",
        "quantizer = faiss.IndexFlatIP(dim)\n",
        "index_ivf = faiss.IndexIVFFlat(quantizer, dim, nlist, faiss.METRIC_INNER_PRODUCT)\n",
        "index_ivf.train(all_item_embs)\n",
        "index_ivf.add(all_item_embs)\n",
        "index_ivf.nprobe = 10\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Faiss indices built: Exact, HNSW, IVF\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Benchmark retrieval\n",
        "import time\n",
        "\n",
        "# Sample queries\n",
        "n_queries = 100\n",
        "query_users = np.random.choice(user_ids, n_queries)\n",
        "query_embs = []\n",
        "for u in query_users:\n",
        "    u_batch = {\n",
        "        'user_id': np.array([u]),\n",
        "        'age': np.array([user_age[u]], dtype=np.float32),\n",
        "        'gender': np.array([user_gender[u]], dtype=np.int64),\n",
        "        'genre_prefs': user_genre_prefs[u:u+1].astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    emb = user_model(u_batch).numpy().astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    faiss.normalize_L2(emb)\n",
        "    query_embs.append(emb)\n",
        "\n",
        "query_embs = np.vstack(query_embs)\n",
        "\n",
        "k = 10\n",
        "\n",
        "# Exact search\n",
        "start = time.time()\n",
        "D_exact, I_exact = index_exact.search(query_embs, k)\n",
        "exact_time = time.time() - start\n",
        "\n",
        "# HNSW search\n",
        "start = time.time()\n",
        "D_hnsw, I_hnsw = index_hnsw.search(query_embs, k)\n",
        "hnsw_time = time.time() - start\n",
        "\n",
        "# IVF search\n",
        "start = time.time()\n",
        "D_ivf, I_ivf = index_ivf.search(query_embs, k)\n",
        "ivf_time = time.time() - start\n",
        "\n",
        "# Recall@10: overlap with exact\n",
        "recall_hnsw = np.mean([len(set(I_hnsw[i]) & set(I_exact[i])) / k for i in range(n_queries)])\n",
        "recall_ivf = np.mean([len(set(I_ivf[i]) & set(I_exact[i])) / k for i in range(n_queries)])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Exact (FlatIP):   {exact_time*1000:.1f} ms total, {exact_time*1000/n_queries:.2f} ms/query\")\n",
        "print(f\"HNSW:             {hnsw_time*1000:.1f} ms total, {hnsw_time*1000/n_queries:.2f} ms/query, Recall@10: {recall_hnsw:.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"IVF (nprobe=10):   {ivf_time*1000:.1f} ms total, {ivf_time*1000/n_queries:.2f} ms/query, Recall@10: {recall_ivf:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Ranking Model: Fine-Grained Scoring\n",
        "\n",
        "Retrieval gives top-K candidates (e.g., 100-1000). Ranking model scores them precisely using richer features (cross features, interaction history)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Ranking model: takes user + item features, outputs score\n",
        "class RankingModel(tf.keras.Model):\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        # User tower (shared with retrieval or separate)\n",
        "        self.user_embedding = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.StringLookup(vocabulary=user_ids_vocab, mask_token=None),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Embedding(len(user_ids_vocab) + 1, 64)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        self.item_embedding = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.StringLookup(vocabulary=item_ids_vocab, mask_token=None),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Embedding(len(item_ids_vocab) + 1, 64)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Cross features\n",
        "        self.cross_layer = tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu')\n",
        "        \n        "        # Scoring head\n",
        "        self.score_head = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(128, activation='relu'),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.2),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu'),\n",
        "            tf.keras.layers.Dense(1)\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def call(self, inputs):\n",
        "        user_emb = self.user_embedding(inputs['user_id'])\n",
        "        item_emb = self.item_embedding(inputs['item_id'])\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Element-wise product (cross)\n",
        "        cross = user_emb * item_emb\n",
        "        cross = self.cross_layer(cross)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Concat: user + item + cross\n",
        "        x = tf.concat([user_emb, item_emb, cross], axis=1)\n",
        "        return self.score_head(x)\n",
        "\n",
        "# TFRS Ranking Task\n",
        "class RankingTask(tfrs.Model):\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.ranking_model = RankingModel()\n",
        "        self.task = tfrs.tasks.Ranking(\n",
        "            loss=tf.keras.losses.BinaryCrossentropy(from_logits=True),\n",
        "            metrics=[\n",
        "                tf.keras.metrics.BinaryAccuracy(threshold=0.0),\n",
        "                tf.keras.metrics.AUC(curve='ROC'),\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def call(self, features):\n",
        "        return self.ranking_model(features)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    def compute_loss(self, features, training=False):\n",
        "        labels = features.pop('label')\n",
        "        scores = self(features)\n",
        "        return self.task(labels, scores, compute_metrics=not training)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Generate training data for ranking (positive + negative samples)\n",
        "def generate_ranking_data(interactions_df, n_neg=4):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Generate (user, item, label) triples with negative sampling\"\"\"\n",
        "    user_item_set = set(zip(interactions_df['user_id'], interactions_df['item_id']))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    ranking_data = []\n",
        "    for _, row in interactions_df.iterrows():\n",
        "        u, i = row['user_id'], row['item_id']\n",
        "        ranking_data.append((u, i, 1.0))  # positive\n",
        "        \n        "        # Negative samples\n",
        "        for _ in range(n_neg):\n",
        "            neg_i = np.random.randint(0, n_items)\n",
        "            while (u, neg_i) in user_item_set:\n",
        "                neg_i = np.random.randint(0, n_items)\n",
        "            ranking_data.append((u, neg_i, 0.0))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(ranking_data, columns=['user_id', 'item_id', 'label'])\n",
        "\n",
        "ranking_df = generate_ranking_data(interactions_df.sample(20000, random_state=42), n_neg=4)\n",
        "print(f\"Ranking data: {len(ranking_df)} samples, positive rate: {ranking_df['label'].mean():.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split\n",
        "rank_train, rank_test = train_test_split(ranking_df, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "rank_train_ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices({\n",
        "    'user_id': rank_train['user_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'item_id': rank_train['item_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'label': rank_train['label'].values.astype(np.float32)\n",
        "}).shuffle(10000).batch(1024).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
        "\n",
        "rank_test_ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices({\n",
        "    'user_id': rank_test['user_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'item_id': rank_test['item_id'].values.astype(np.int64),\n",
        "    'label': rank_test['label'].values.astype(np.float32)\n",
        "}).batch(1024).prefetch(tf.data.AUTOTUNE)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Train ranking model\n",
        "ranking_model = RankingTask()\n",
        "ranking_model.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-3))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Training ranking model...\")\n",
        "ranking_model.fit(rank_train_ds, epochs=3, verbose=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nEvaluating ranking...\")\n",
        "ranking_model.evaluate(rank_test_ds, verbose=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. End-to-End Retrieval + Ranking Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def recommend(user_id, k_retrieve=100, k_rank=10):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Two-stage recommendation: retrieve -> rerank\"\"\"\n",
        "    # Stage 1: Retrieval via Faiss HNSW\n",
        "    u_batch = {\n",
        "        'user_id': np.array([user_id]),\n",
        "        'age': np.array([user_age[user_id]], dtype=np.float32),\n",
        "        'gender': np.array([user_gender[user_id]], dtype=np.int64),\n",
        "        'genre_prefs': user_genre_prefs[user_id:user_id+1].astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    user_emb = user_model(u_batch).numpy().astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    faiss.normalize_L2(user_emb)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    D, I = index_hnsw.search(user_emb, k_retrieve)\n",
        "    candidate_ids = I[0]\n",
        "    \n        # Stage 2: Ranking\n",
        "    rank_inputs = {\n",
        "        'user_id': np.full(k_retrieve, user_id, dtype=np.int64),\n",
        "        'item_id': candidate_ids.astype(np.int64)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    scores = ranking_model(rank_inputs).numpy().flatten()\n",
        "    \n        # Top-K after reranking\n",
        "    top_k_idx = np.argsort(scores)[::-1][:k_rank]\n",
        "    \n        "    return candidate_ids[top_k_idx], scores[top_k_idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Test recommendation\n",
        "test_user = 42\n",
        "rec_items, rec_scores = recommend(test_user, k_retrieve=100, k_rank=10)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Top 10 recommendations for user {test_user}:\")\n",
        "for i, (item_id, score) in enumerate(zip(rec_items, rec_scores)):\n",
        "    print(f\"  {i+1}. Item {item_id}: score={score:.4f}, popularity={item_popularity[item_id]:.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Evaluation: Recall@K, NDCG@K, Coverage, Diversity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def evaluate_recommender(test_interactions, k_values=[5, 10, 20, 50]):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Evaluate retrieval + ranking pipeline\"\"\"\n",
        "    # Group test interactions by user\n",
        "    test_by_user = test_interactions.groupby('user_id')['item_id'].apply(list).to_dict()\n",
        "    \n        "    results = {k: {'recall': [], 'ndcg': []} for k in k_values}\n",
        "    all_recommended = set()\n",
        "    \n",
        "    for user_id, true_items in test_by_user.items():\n",
        "        if user_id >= n_users:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "            \n        "        rec_items, _ = recommend(user_id, k_retrieve=200, k_rank=max(k_values))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        for k in k_values:\n",
        "            top_k = rec_items[:k]\n",
        "            all_recommended.update(top_k)\n",
        "            \n        "            # Recall@K\n",
        "            hits = len(set(top_k) & set(true_items))\n",
        "            recall = hits / len(true_items) if true_items else 0\n",
        "            results[k]['recall'].append(recall)\n",
        "            \n        "            # NDCG@K\n",
        "            relevance = [1.0 if item in true_items else 0.0 for item in top_k]\n",
        "            if sum(relevance) > 0:\n",
        "                ndcg = ndcg_score([relevance], [list(range(len(relevance), 0, -1))])\n",
        "                results[k]['ndcg'].append(ndcg)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                results[k]['ndcg'].append(0.0)\n",
        "    \n        "    # Coverage: fraction of items ever recommended\n",
        "    coverage = len(all_recommended) / n_items\n",
        "    \n        "    # Diversity: average pairwise dissimilarity in top-K\n",
        "    # (using genre vectors)\n",
        "    \n        "    return results, coverage\n",
        "\n",
        "# Evaluate on test users\n",
        "test_users = interactions_df['user_id'].unique()\n",
        "test_interactions_sample = interactions_df[interactions_df['user_id'].isin(test_users[:500])]\n",
        "\n",
        "eval_results, coverage = evaluate_recommender(test_interactions_sample)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Coverage: {coverage:.3f}\")\n",
        "for k in [5, 10, 20, 50]:\n",
        "    print(f\"K={k}: Recall={np.mean(eval_results[k]['recall']):.4f}, NDCG={np.mean(eval_results[k]['ndcg']):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
